::  name       lantern face stone-edge theme
::  shape      a style: layer that recolors the face's unknown marker (edge) only
::  invariant  the edge token stays warm/low-blue; head and flow inherit from the base
::  example    an unknown marker in warm stone rather than the base's warm rule
::  readers    brush_parse.rye -> tokens.resolve -> lantern_face_theme
::  nib        lantern-face-theme-v0
::
::  A .brush theme for the asking voice's face: it names only the `edge` token --
::  the color the honest i-don't-know marker wears -- and leaves head (settled)
::  and flow (proposed) to inherit from the base sheet, proving the cascade
::  recolors one settledness without touching its siblings.
::  Tongue: Glow · Bron · TAME · Radiant. Never JS · HTML · CSS · JSON.
::
::  at-nib:     lantern-face-stone-edge
::  present:    Frame
::  max-lines:  8
::  style:
::    edge 0xFFB08A5A
::  lines:
::    lantern face, stone edge theme
::  refuse:     src/web · Wasm/Web backend · CSS rail · a { } stylesheet
